## Metal–Organic Frameworks
Precise Modulation of the Breathing Behavior and Pore Surface in $Z{\mathsf{r}}.$ -MOFs by Reversible Post-Synthetic Variable-Spacer Installation to Fine-Tune the Expansion Magnitude and Sorption Properties
Bringing PSM into dynamic MOFs: Postsynthetic modification (PSM) is used to install/uninstall varied linkers into/from a flexible Zr-MOF. This post-synthetic variable-spacer installation (PVSI) strategy is used to tune elastic deformation, breathing behavior, and stabilization of the framework in controllable and predictable way. Tuning the pore surface leads to a larger surface area and improved gas separation and adsorption capacity.
